# autodemo — environment configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# autodemo needs NO API keys and NO credentials. It runs entirely on your
# machine: a local browser, a local encoder, and a local or public TTS voice.
# You can run the whole project without ever creating a .env file.
#
# Everything that matters is configured in autodemo.config.yaml instead. The
# variables below are optional overrides only.
#
#   1. Copy this file to '.env' if you need any of them: cp .env.example .env
#   2. NEVER commit a real '.env'.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Browser ---
# Path to the Chrome/Chromium/Edge executable used to record. Overrides
# `app.chromePath` in the config. Leave unset to auto-detect, which falls back
# to Playwright's bundled chromium.
# CHROME_PATH=C:/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe

# --- Logging ---
# Reserved for future verbosity control (debug, info, warn, error).
# AUTODEMO_LOG=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT used by autodemo, listed only to prevent confusion:
#
#   The examples/map-app config points at a public deployment of a separate
#   map application. That app needs a Mapbox token — but the token belongs to
#   *that app's* own deployment, not to autodemo. Nothing here reads it, and
#   no token should ever be placed in this file.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
